WEBVTT

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:16.490
Polar Bear's Café

00:01:29.980 --> 00:01:34.940
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:01:31.380 --> 00:01:33.700
Panda's Apology!

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.050
Miss Sasako,

00:01:37.050 --> 00:01:40.330
I want to try something other 
than a café mocha sometime.

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:42.000
What do you suggest?

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.660
Let's see...

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.050
I think a café mocha 
is perfectly fine.

00:01:46.540 --> 00:01:49.910
Could you think about it a 
little longer, Miss Sasako?

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:50.790
It's done.

00:01:51.420 --> 00:01:52.370
What is?

00:01:52.370 --> 00:01:55.200
I've been thinking about 
adding this to the menu.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.090
Want to try it? It's crab bread.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:01:58.890
Crab bread?

00:01:59.950 --> 00:02:01.810
Sure, I'll give it a shot.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.510
Just came out of the oven.

00:02:07.520 --> 00:02:09.140
You know,

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:12.030
I don't know that "realism" is really an important factor for bread.

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:14.650
Would a red king crab 
have been better?

00:02:14.650 --> 00:02:16.210
I don't think the species is the issue.

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:17.910
I think it's the presentation.

00:02:24.430 --> 00:02:26.610
What's the matter, Panda?

00:02:26.610 --> 00:02:29.890
I really don't want 
to go to work today.

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:33.230
Will you go to work 
for me, Mr. Penguin?

00:02:33.660 --> 00:02:36.380
You say that all year long, don't you?

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:40.050
Usually it's a normal feeling 
of not wanting to go,

00:02:40.050 --> 00:02:43.000
but I <i>really</i> don't want to go today.

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:46.950
"Oh, okay sure. Well, in that 
case, I'll totally go for you!"

00:02:46.950 --> 00:02:50.810
Do you think there's anybody in the world who'd say that?

00:02:55.410 --> 00:03:00.240
I fling off 
my blue bandana...

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.240
Apparently there was someone, and they were very close by.

00:03:04.090 --> 00:03:07.850
You need to make sure 
you thank Polar Bear.

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:10.040
Okay, I will.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:11.870
So exciting.

00:03:13.320 --> 00:03:14.340
Stop right there.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:17.520
Is there a problem?

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:19.380
What is your name?

00:03:20.360 --> 00:03:21.540
It's Panda.

00:03:23.330 --> 00:03:24.850
What's that?

00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:30.230
So, what is your name?

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:31.770
It's Panda.

00:03:32.340 --> 00:03:35.480
There's no way a panda 
would look like...

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:39.790
See?

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.990
Could I please see your 
license <i>(menkyosho)</i>?

00:03:43.850 --> 00:03:44.490
What?

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:46.830
A gold dust show <i>(kinpunshou)</i>?

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:48.120
Your license <i>(menkyosho)</i>.

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:50.340
A falconer <i>(takajou)</i>?

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.120
Your license <i>(menkyosho)</i>.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:55.420
Tuna Butchering Demo

00:03:53.250 --> 00:03:55.420
A tuna butchering demo 
<i>(maguro kaitaishou)</i>?

00:03:56.090 --> 00:03:57.420
Your license!

00:03:57.990 --> 00:03:59.860
You're a very diligent worker.

00:03:59.860 --> 00:04:01.470
Thank you.

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.300
You're Polar Bear.

00:04:07.650 --> 00:04:08.980
I am Polar Bear.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:16.320
Please stop wasting our time.

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:18.150
I'm terribly sorry.

00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:21.570
Come on, Mr. Polar Bear. 
You too.

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:23.770
I'm very sorry.

00:04:27.190 --> 00:04:30.540
This is why I said you 
shouldn't do it.

00:04:31.070 --> 00:04:33.370
I'll make sure to walk next time.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:36.120
That's not the issue here.

00:04:36.680 --> 00:04:38.880
So, what's Panda doing?

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.510
He got a phone call from Mr. Handa

00:04:41.510 --> 00:04:43.590
and went to the zoo.

00:04:45.790 --> 00:04:48.050
I'm sorry, Polar Bear.

00:04:48.410 --> 00:04:50.110
It's no problem at all.

00:04:50.110 --> 00:04:52.020
It's not your fault, Panda.

00:04:52.530 --> 00:04:57.610
Hey, since you were imprisoned...

00:04:57.610 --> 00:04:59.140
You mean questioned 
by the police?

00:04:59.140 --> 00:05:00.490
Yeah.

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:03.490
Since you were questioned 
by the police...

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:07.270
As an apology, I'll work 
at the café tomorrow.

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.330
So you should take the 
day off, Polar Bear.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:12.310
Oh?

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:16.380
Okay? Take it easy, Polar Bear.

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:19.500
What's with you all a sudden, Panda?

00:05:19.500 --> 00:05:21.840
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.550
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:30.220
All right, I'll be off, then.

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:31.920
See ya!

00:05:31.920 --> 00:05:35.020
Are you really going, Mr. Polar Bear?

00:05:35.730 --> 00:05:39.190
Everything will be fine 
if we leave it to Panda.

00:05:39.800 --> 00:05:41.400
You're enjoying this, aren't you?

00:05:43.160 --> 00:05:44.330
I'm leaving everything to you.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:45.940
Okay.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:51.210
See ya!

00:05:51.210 --> 00:05:53.050
Why the hell are you drinking?

00:05:53.050 --> 00:05:56.070
That means I have to 
drive the whole time!

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:57.160
Guess I've got no choice.

00:06:00.080 --> 00:06:02.130
Have a safe trip!

00:06:03.830 --> 00:06:06.770
Miss Sasako, let's do our best.

00:06:07.250 --> 00:06:07.760
Yes.

00:06:11.790 --> 00:06:13.140
Welcome.

00:06:13.410 --> 00:06:17.000
Oh, you were serious about 
working here part-time, Panda?

00:06:17.000 --> 00:06:18.870
Just for a day.

00:06:19.310 --> 00:06:22.520
I'm going to be relaxing even 
more than usual starting tomorrow.

00:06:23.970 --> 00:06:26.570
I don't think you need 
to announce that.

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.710
But I'm going to work hard today.

00:06:33.300 --> 00:06:35.120
What would you like?

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.580
My usual, please.

00:06:38.370 --> 00:06:40.460
Here you go, have some water.

00:06:41.540 --> 00:06:42.700
Please take your time.

00:06:43.780 --> 00:06:47.150
Panda, I can't even 
count how many times

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:49.240
I've had a café mocha 
in front of you.

00:06:49.840 --> 00:06:51.440
I'll make one right now.

00:07:03.880 --> 00:07:06.150
There doesn't seem to be any 
customers coming today.

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.310
Indeed.

00:07:11.930 --> 00:07:13.730
I wonder if they're closed.

00:07:13.730 --> 00:07:15.990
Looks like it. Let's try another day.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:25.050
What? The doors are locked.

00:07:25.680 --> 00:07:27.240
Oh, that.

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:29.830
If I unlocked the doors, 
customers would come in,

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:31.260
so I kept them locked.

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:32.010
Wha?

00:07:33.120 --> 00:07:37.430
Polar Bear is always saying 
how busy he is, right?

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:39.510
I see.

00:07:39.510 --> 00:07:41.390
I appreciate the concern,

00:07:41.390 --> 00:07:43.280
but let's keep the doors unlocked.

00:07:43.280 --> 00:07:44.520
Okay.

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:47.450
So it's better if 
customers come, right?

00:07:47.450 --> 00:07:49.440
Then if we get customers,

00:07:49.440 --> 00:07:51.920
how much should we make the 
customers do themselves?

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:56.090
Um, we usually do it all ourselves.

00:07:56.730 --> 00:07:59.110
What is this conversation?

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.580
Do you have any seats open?

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:08.840
Yes, but you'd be sharing a 
table with someone else.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:09.900
Is that all right?

00:08:09.900 --> 00:08:10.760
Yes.

00:08:12.750 --> 00:08:14.220
Here you go.

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:15.680
Pull up a chair.

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:20.140
I apologize.

00:08:20.140 --> 00:08:23.320
We'll show you to another seat 
as soon as one opens up.

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:30.350
Please take your time.

00:08:31.190 --> 00:08:32.850
Could you take our order, please?

00:08:33.360 --> 00:08:35.740
Oh, okay. I'll be right with you.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:39.030
Don't forget about the 
food, too, Panda.

00:08:39.530 --> 00:08:41.040
Okay.

00:09:15.060 --> 00:09:16.950
Thank you very much.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:18.370
I'm serious.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:21.040
Oh, stop it, you.

00:09:21.630 --> 00:09:23.560
Well, see you later, Grannie.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:24.800
Indeed.

00:09:31.420 --> 00:09:33.170
Oh, Mr. Polar Bear.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:35.360
Welcome back.

00:09:35.950 --> 00:09:36.880
Thanks.

00:09:37.290 --> 00:09:38.990
See ya, Polar Bear.

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:40.680
See you later.

00:09:45.280 --> 00:09:47.130
Oh, welcome back.

00:09:47.130 --> 00:09:48.460
Thanks.

00:09:48.460 --> 00:09:49.960
Where's Panda?

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.270
He's here.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:55.280
Panda worked really 
hard all day today.

00:09:55.830 --> 00:09:58.400
Even when Mr. Penguin offered to help,

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.370
he kept saying he'd do it himself.

00:10:00.810 --> 00:10:04.550
Then I noticed that I haven't 
heard him in a while...

00:10:04.900 --> 00:10:05.680
Look.

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:14.720
Panda.

00:10:15.590 --> 00:10:16.260
It's fine.

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:19.150
I told you everything would be okay

00:10:19.150 --> 00:10:21.100
if we left it up to Panda.

00:10:21.730 --> 00:10:22.600
Indeed.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.980
You can relax, Polar Bear.

00:10:35.410 --> 00:10:37.950
You don't need to be 
worried about that.

00:10:47.000 --> 00:10:52.000
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:10:48.400 --> 00:10:50.760
Rin Rin Welcomed!

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:57.000
We're finally done!

00:10:57.890 --> 00:10:59.750
Thanks for your hard work.

00:10:59.750 --> 00:11:01.030
Thank you, too.

00:11:01.030 --> 00:11:01.780
Panda.

00:11:05.700 --> 00:11:07.810
Thanks for your hard work. Here.

00:11:09.760 --> 00:11:10.690
Bye!

00:11:11.250 --> 00:11:12.690
See you later!

00:11:12.690 --> 00:11:14.650
Do your best on Sunday, too!

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:26.370
Miss Sasako.

00:11:26.880 --> 00:11:27.950
What is it?

00:11:28.440 --> 00:11:30.250
If you absolutely insist,

00:11:30.250 --> 00:11:33.460
I'll show you how I get onto a chair.

00:11:33.940 --> 00:11:35.110
I'm sorry,

00:11:35.110 --> 00:11:36.530
but I'm rather busy right now,

00:11:36.530 --> 00:11:37.630
so I'll look if it'll be quick.

00:11:38.250 --> 00:11:39.650
Never mind then.

00:11:39.650 --> 00:11:41.400
I'll do it when you have time.

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:42.480
Mr. Penguin.

00:11:42.480 --> 00:11:44.150
Hmm? What is it?

00:11:44.520 --> 00:11:46.350
If you absolutely insist,

00:11:47.060 --> 00:11:52.690
I'll show you how I catch a walrus, instead of a seal.

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:57.790
I will gladly decline that offer.

00:11:57.790 --> 00:11:58.830
You sure?

00:12:01.130 --> 00:12:02.200
Welcome.

00:12:03.690 --> 00:12:05.880
He gave me flowers again.

00:12:06.400 --> 00:12:07.580
Rin Rin?

00:12:08.330 --> 00:12:12.750
Would you go return these in 
a hurry for me, Mr. Penguin?

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.290
Is there a reason for me to hurry?

00:12:17.320 --> 00:12:20.010
Panda was so cute again today.

00:12:25.420 --> 00:12:26.580
Welcome!

00:12:26.580 --> 00:12:28.850
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:12:28.850 --> 00:12:29.640
Oh, it's fine.

00:12:30.120 --> 00:12:34.140
Um, Mr. Panda asked me to 
give you this letter.

00:12:34.570 --> 00:12:36.560
What? From Panda?

00:12:36.960 --> 00:12:39.690
Really? Thank you!

00:12:42.290 --> 00:12:45.530
I'll be waiting for you 
at Bird Land at 8 PM.

00:12:47.790 --> 00:12:49.530
I'll be waiting!

00:12:50.720 --> 00:12:52.170
Yay!

00:12:56.670 --> 00:13:00.860
Bird Land

00:13:02.540 --> 00:13:03.870
I hope this is the place.

00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:07.310
Welcome!

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:13.720
Here's your beer!

00:13:16.590 --> 00:13:18.560
Hey there, Mr. Hayashi.

00:13:18.890 --> 00:13:21.550
Oh, Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:25.490
Um, where's Panda?

00:13:26.310 --> 00:13:28.490
Why don't you take a seat?

00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:34.410
Um... I'm supposed to be 
meeting up with Panda.

00:13:37.140 --> 00:13:39.470
Oh, I'm the one that sent that letter.

00:13:39.470 --> 00:13:40.880
I'm the one that invited you.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:42.360
But Panda—

00:13:44.230 --> 00:13:47.080
Oh, Panda this, Panda that...

00:13:47.080 --> 00:13:49.660
I'm a panda, too!

00:13:49.660 --> 00:13:51.050
Come and have a seat.

00:13:51.050 --> 00:13:52.540
Come on.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:53.640
Oh.

00:13:55.420 --> 00:13:57.510
Is beer okay with you, Mr. Hayashi?

00:13:59.020 --> 00:13:59.940
Uh...

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.150
What should I do?

00:14:06.150 --> 00:14:07.540
What's the matter?

00:14:07.540 --> 00:14:08.740
Need some advice?

00:14:08.740 --> 00:14:13.030
I want to share a bit of my cuteness with someone.

00:14:14.050 --> 00:14:17.400
Could I withdraw my 
offer to give advice?

00:14:17.400 --> 00:14:21.560
I'm overflowing with cuteness.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:24.320
Could I get another café 
mocha, Miss Sasako?

00:14:24.760 --> 00:14:25.300
Right.

00:14:26.160 --> 00:14:27.630
Cheers!

00:14:29.090 --> 00:14:30.420
Pardon me, but,

00:14:30.420 --> 00:14:31.710
what exactly did you

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:33.550
want with me, Mr. Full-time Panda?

00:14:34.450 --> 00:14:36.020
Mr. Hayashi.

00:14:36.020 --> 00:14:38.020
We're both pandas,

00:14:38.020 --> 00:14:39.750
but you're always going on and on

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:41.440
about how cute Panda is.

00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:45.660
Why don't you ever call me cute?

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:48.740
Hey, Miss! Could I get 
some dried squid?

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:49.910
Right away!

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:52.400
Could you add on some edamame, too?

00:14:52.400 --> 00:14:53.640
Right away!

00:14:53.640 --> 00:14:56.480
So, why is that?

00:14:57.650 --> 00:14:59.670
I think it's subtle things like that.

00:15:00.260 --> 00:15:02.440
Everything that I do should be cute!

00:15:02.440 --> 00:15:04.000
I'm a panda!

00:15:04.430 --> 00:15:06.030
I wouldn't say that...

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:12.850
Hey, Miss! Could I get 
some dried squid?

00:15:13.650 --> 00:15:14.970
Yeah, he's cute.

00:15:15.410 --> 00:15:18.330
What are you grinning 
about, Mr. Hayashi?

00:15:18.330 --> 00:15:20.350
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:15:20.350 --> 00:15:22.010
I was imagining Panda saying that line,

00:15:22.010 --> 00:15:23.190
and it was really cute.

00:15:24.680 --> 00:15:27.110
What's so different?

00:15:27.110 --> 00:15:28.780
We're both pandas!

00:15:31.070 --> 00:15:32.640
Do you want to see?

00:15:32.640 --> 00:15:34.450
It's a photo album of Panda.

00:15:34.450 --> 00:15:36.830
Do you always carry that around?

00:15:36.830 --> 00:15:39.870
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:15:40.580 --> 00:15:43.120
I wanted to go through 
it with Panda today,

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:44.270
so I brought it.

00:15:44.680 --> 00:15:46.800
See? Look how cute he is.

00:15:47.210 --> 00:15:50.170
Yeah, he is cute. And me?

00:15:51.130 --> 00:15:54.800
Well, I think you look a bit tired.

00:15:55.510 --> 00:15:58.020
Yeah, I look exhausted.

00:15:58.530 --> 00:16:00.360
Here's a picture of Panda with bedhead

00:16:00.360 --> 00:16:02.310
after being sucked up by a vacuum.

00:16:03.340 --> 00:16:04.720
Isn't he cute?

00:16:05.100 --> 00:16:07.100
Yeah, he's cute.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:07.730
And me?

00:16:08.660 --> 00:16:09.690
Well...

00:16:10.270 --> 00:16:12.200
You're doing a side job.

00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:14.660
You can get a sense of how he lives from that picture.

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:16.370
Oh, hi there, Llama.

00:16:16.810 --> 00:16:18.620
May I join you two?

00:16:18.620 --> 00:16:20.360
Of course, of course!

00:16:20.360 --> 00:16:22.210
Here, have a drink.

00:16:22.450 --> 00:16:23.540
Thank you very much.

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:27.760
At least you get pictures 
taken of you.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:30.870
Everyone always passes right by me.

00:16:30.870 --> 00:16:33.550
Oh, so you work at the zoo, too?

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:37.380
See? That's what I mean.

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:40.930
Polar 
Bear's 
Café

00:16:41.570 --> 00:16:43.450
Here's your beer and dried squid.

00:16:43.450 --> 00:16:45.480
Took long enough!

00:16:45.480 --> 00:16:46.900
Sorry!

00:16:48.850 --> 00:16:51.370
I don't think that's a good ide—

00:16:51.370 --> 00:16:53.310
Hey, Rin Rin!

00:16:53.790 --> 00:16:54.360
Yes?

00:16:56.010 --> 00:16:59.450
You must be really popular.

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:01.650
You don't handle alcohol well, do you?

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.340
Well, yes, I am.

00:17:03.840 --> 00:17:05.040
Not very humble...

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:09.960
I want to be seen as 
cute, Mr. Rin Ran.

00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:12.350
It's Rin Rin.

00:17:12.830 --> 00:17:15.710
Are you all right, 
Mr. Full-time Panda?

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:18.150
Come to the zoo tomorrow.

00:17:18.150 --> 00:17:20.680
But Panda won't be there tomorrow.

00:17:21.210 --> 00:17:23.520
But I'll be there!

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:25.310
Me, too.

00:17:25.780 --> 00:17:27.750
You better come tomorrow.

00:17:28.410 --> 00:17:31.230
All right, I'll go.

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:36.300
Thank you, Mr. Rin Ron.

00:17:37.320 --> 00:17:38.400
It's Rin Rin.

00:17:43.870 --> 00:17:45.380
Hello.

00:17:45.380 --> 00:17:47.120
Hey, Mr. Hayashi.

00:17:47.790 --> 00:17:50.010
Thank you very much.

00:17:50.530 --> 00:17:55.030
I do think that pandas 
are cute in general...

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.270
So I wonder why you aren't

00:17:58.270 --> 00:18:00.180
that cute, Mr. Full-time Panda...

00:18:01.200 --> 00:18:02.680
Why indeed?

00:18:04.830 --> 00:18:05.770
What's that?

00:18:07.030 --> 00:18:09.330
Oh, it's my side job.

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:11.360
I'll finish it up real quick.

00:18:11.360 --> 00:18:12.980
Mr. Full-time Panda!

00:18:13.290 --> 00:18:15.120
I can get through it quite quickly

00:18:15.120 --> 00:18:16.980
when there aren't any customers around.

00:18:16.980 --> 00:18:18.860
How about you stop that?

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.960
Pandas doing side jobs aren't cute.

00:18:21.960 --> 00:18:22.910
Really?

00:18:23.840 --> 00:18:26.660
Heave-ho, heave-ho.

00:18:27.770 --> 00:18:29.080
Yeah, he's cute.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:33.090
I wonder if it's a matter 
of potential...

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:34.240
Hey,

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:35.710
don't give up on me.

00:18:36.250 --> 00:18:37.350
Well then,

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:39.960
how about we have you 
play with a tire?

00:18:39.960 --> 00:18:41.600
Sure...

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:48.480
How's that?

00:18:49.880 --> 00:18:53.420
It's cute, but only slightly.

00:18:54.300 --> 00:18:57.690
Oh, I'm sorry! But you'll be fine!

00:18:57.690 --> 00:18:59.320
You're a panda!

00:18:59.320 --> 00:19:00.630
Thanks...

00:19:01.200 --> 00:19:04.130
I wonder if I'll be okay 
being only slightly cute.

00:19:09.270 --> 00:19:12.890
I feel bad for what I did 
to Mr. Full-time Panda.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:14.800
Pardon...

00:19:16.600 --> 00:19:19.170
Oh, Mr. Llama! I'm sorry!

00:19:19.170 --> 00:19:20.860
I was just looking for you.

00:19:20.860 --> 00:19:24.100
I didn't forget about you... at all!

00:19:32.320 --> 00:19:34.250
So cute!

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:42.570
Panda!

00:19:49.270 --> 00:19:51.460
Do your best, Mr. Panda!

00:20:07.750 --> 00:20:09.180
Look over here!

00:20:09.180 --> 00:20:10.750
So cute!

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:13.850
I guess I can't beat Panda.

00:20:17.200 --> 00:20:19.640
I'm finally done!

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:22.990
Thanks for your hard work, Panda!

00:20:22.990 --> 00:20:23.850
Here, take this!

00:20:24.420 --> 00:20:26.300
But...

00:20:26.300 --> 00:20:28.240
Mr. Panda!

00:20:28.240 --> 00:20:31.440
Um, will you take a cell 
phone picture with us?

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:33.360
Sure.

00:20:33.360 --> 00:20:35.240
Yay! Thank you.

00:20:35.240 --> 00:20:37.940
A panda holding flowers is so cute!

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:39.560
Thanks!

00:20:39.560 --> 00:20:42.040
Do your best next week, too!

00:20:43.380 --> 00:20:45.510
He really is popular.

00:20:45.970 --> 00:20:47.260
Well, he is cute.

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:49.100
Thanks for your hard work.

00:20:52.890 --> 00:20:53.980
Um...

00:20:56.920 --> 00:20:58.180
Mr. Panda!

00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:02.200
Oh, Panda already le—

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.140
No, not him.

00:21:05.110 --> 00:21:06.160
Huh?

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:08.550
I wanted to see you!

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:13.960
Here!

00:21:18.490 --> 00:21:19.550
For me?

00:21:20.010 --> 00:21:21.010
Yup!

00:21:22.990 --> 00:21:24.210
See ya!

00:21:27.430 --> 00:21:30.150
I got to give them 
to Mr. Panda, Mommy!

00:21:31.220 --> 00:21:32.760
Really? Good for you.

00:21:32.760 --> 00:21:33.710
Yeah!

00:21:34.320 --> 00:21:35.560
See ya!

00:21:36.040 --> 00:21:37.700
Bye-bye!

00:21:41.450 --> 00:21:43.570
Bye-bye!

00:22:04.570 --> 00:22:05.720
Mr. Penguin!

00:22:06.940 --> 00:22:08.680
What is it, Miss Sasako?

00:22:08.680 --> 00:22:12.010
I'll watch you as you sit! 
Very attentively!

00:22:12.500 --> 00:22:13.290
Huh?

00:22:15.410 --> 00:22:16.390
So exciting!

00:22:17.080 --> 00:22:20.400
It's not that big of a deal.

00:22:20.400 --> 00:22:22.200
Let's do it another time.

00:22:22.720 --> 00:22:23.640
'Kay?

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:59.980
Next Time

00:23:58.260 --> 00:23:59.870
Mr. Penguin, Mr. Penguin.

00:23:59.870 --> 00:24:01.170
What is it, Panda?

00:24:01.170 --> 00:24:03.750
Tell us the first thing 
that comes to mind.

00:24:03.750 --> 00:24:07.210
When you miss the chorus of a song by a little bit when you're singing karaoke,

00:24:07.210 --> 00:24:09.870
how do you recover without embarrassing yourself?

00:24:09.870 --> 00:24:11.940
Talk about it more passionately.

00:24:11.940 --> 00:24:13.240
About this?

00:24:13.240 --> 00:24:15.340
It's something I'd rather 
talk about quietly.

00:24:15.340 --> 00:24:17.310
Actually, let's end this, Polar Bear.

00:24:17.530 --> 00:24:19.630
Next week's Polar Bear's Café

00:24:19.630 --> 00:24:21.230
will be presented in bits and pieces.

00:24:21.230 --> 00:24:22.750
We'll be presenting the whole thing!

00:24:21.810 --> 00:24:24.220
Panda's New Part-time Job
Mr. Penguin Goes Flying

00:24:22.750 --> 00:24:24.220
Enjoy!
